# Internationalization

## Rules

- Messages live in `messages/<locale>.json` at the root. Add each key to every locale in the same change.
- Follow the key style already in `messages/en.json`. Group keys per feature, at most three levels deep.
- No hardcoded user-facing strings, including `alt`, `aria-label` and metadata.
- Keys are checked by the library's type support, so a missing key is a type error. Never build keys from variables.
- Read the locale from the library, never from `window.location` or by parsing the URL.

<!-- nextjs:start -->
## next-intl

- `useTranslations` in Client Components and sync Server Components; `getTranslations` in async server code and `generateMetadata`.
- Routing config, `Link`, `redirect` and `useRouter` come from `@/i18n/routing`, not from `next/navigation`.
- Register the message type in next-intl's `AppConfig` so keys are type-checked.
<!-- nextjs:end -->
<!-- tanstack:start -->
## Paraglide JS

- Each key is a function: `import * as m from "@/paraglide/messages.js"`, then `m.cart_title()`.
- The locale comes from `@/paraglide/runtime.js` (`getLocale`, `setLocale`).
- `src/paraglide/` is generated on install and build. Never edit it; change `messages/` or `project.inlang/settings.json`.
<!-- tanstack:end -->

<incorrect-example>
```tsx
<button>Log in</button>
<p>{t(`status_${status}`)}</p>
```
</incorrect-example>
